        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-6",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Right dorsal foot lump, patient-reported"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Lump near the base of the fourth toe is still present and a bit annoying in enclosed shoes, especially cheap flats. Mild tenderness only when a shoe rubs; no pain at rest, itch, discharge, ulceration, or noticed colour change. Onset unclear; noticed this term, possibly last term. Subjectively stable in size, possibly slightly increased, but patient is unsure."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-7",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-7",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Right dorsal foot skin finding"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "At the base of the fourth toe, an approximately 6–7 mm firm, well-circumscribed, slightly raised dermal papule with a tan-brown colour and smooth surface. Positive dimple sign on lateral compression."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-8",
